NAME
  kill - send a signal to a process or process group

SYNOPSIS
  kill [-s SIGNAL | -SIGNAL] PID...

DESCRIPTION
  Sends SIGNAL (default TERM) to each PID. A negative id targets
  the process group with that pgid, POSIX kill(-pgid) style.

  Signals: TERM, KILL, INT, STOP, CONT, 0 (check existence only),
  or a signal number. TERM exits 143, KILL 137, INT 130.
  STOP suspends a process (scheduler takes no CPU for it); CONT
  resumes it. Only root or the same uid may signal a process.

EXAMPLES
  kill 42
    Terminate pid 42.

  kill -KILL 42
    Kill pid 42 immediately.

  kill -0 42
    Check pid 42 exists.

  kill -- -7
    Terminate every process in group 7.

